## The runtime

The game is built on the {{engine.name}} engine, which documents itself in
the `engine/` directory at the root of this repository. It is a gameplay
framework as much as a runtime: the game is written as subclasses of its
classes, a game instance, a game mode, actors and their components, and the
controllers that drive them, and the engine constructs, ticks, and renders
them in a fixed order. It owns the frame loop and the delta time the game is
given, rendering and the camera, the canvas fit, the input actions the menus
and editor verbs are driven by, the pointer the editor and the menus are
operated with, audio cues, asset loading, and the debug overlay. Read its
documentation before you start. This specification states only what is
specific to Orrery.

The logical design field handed to the engine is the stage, and the game
leaves the camera at rest, so world units and the stage's logical units
coincide and every position in this specification is both. The pointer
reaches the game from the engine already in those units, as ordered samples
carrying its press and release edges. `specs/controls.md` states what Orrery
does with them.
{{/if}}

